# SPECTRA - .tool-versions (asdf / mise format)
#
# Status: session one. This file is the thing being delivered. Every toolchain
# it names is "not started" as far as source in this repository goes.
#
# Scope: Tier A only (Part II section 73.1) - Rust, Go, Python, TypeScript,
# SQL, Bash. Tier B, C and D toolchains are NOT pinned here. They live in
# spectra/toolchain-b, -c and -d and are reached through those images
# (Part II section 74.1); pinning them on the host would invite a local install
# that never matches the image and would break the "no per-language image, no
# host resolver" posture.
#
# THE BINDING RULE. Every line below must match the toolchain baked into
# spectra/toolchain-a at the digest recorded in images.lock. This file is the
# convenience copy for a developer working in WSL2 outside the container; the
# image is the authority. `make doctor` will compare found-vs-pinned and exit
# nonzero on any mismatch once that comparison is implemented; today it probes
# presence only (Part I section 33, target table). If a version here and the
# image disagree, the image wins and this file is the bug.
#
# No line may ever read `latest`, `stable`, `nightly`, or carry a range
# operator (`^`, `~`, `*`, `>=`) - Part II section 74.11.2.
#
# Versions below are the pins stated in Part I section 33.6. They are pins,
# not measurements, and nothing here is a claim that any of them has been run.

# --- Python: generator, ingest orchestration, ER, API services -------------
# Must match spectra/toolchain-a at the images.lock digest.
# Members under python/ pin requires-python = "==3.12.*"; uv.lock will be
# committed once a dependency exists, and is absent while there are none.
python 3.12.7

# --- Rust: proof kernel, grounder, fixpoint, cut solver --------------------
# Must match spectra/toolchain-a at the images.lock digest.
# rust-toolchain.toml is the in-tree authority for channel, components and the
# wasm32-unknown-unknown target; this line exists so `mise install` on a bare
# WSL2 host lands on the same compiler.
rust 1.82.0

# --- Go: the independent `spectra verify` checker --------------------------
# Must match spectra/toolchain-a at the images.lock digest.
golang 1.23.2

# --- TypeScript toolchain: frontend, proof UX, demo pane -------------------
# Must match spectra/toolchain-a at the images.lock digest.
nodejs 20.17.0
# Must match spectra/toolchain-a at the images.lock digest; also pinned by the
# root package.json `packageManager` field, and the two must agree.
pnpm 9.12.0

# --- SQL: fact-base schema, recursive-CTE state view, migrations -----------
# Must match spectra/toolchain-a at the images.lock digest. This pin is the
# psql client used by migrations and the state view; the server version is
# pinned separately by digest in docker/compose.core.yml.
postgres 16.4

# --- Bash: the shell layer under every make target -------------------------
# NOT pinned here. Bash 5 is provided by spectra/toolchain-a and by the WSL2
# distribution image pinned in docs/dev/wsl.md. asdf/mise shimming the shell
# that runs the shims is a loop nobody should build.
# `make doctor` asserts bash >= 5 and must match spectra/toolchain-a at the
# images.lock digest.
#
# TODO(decision): make, git, jq and blake3 are also Tier A dependencies and are
# likewise unpinned here for the same reason - they come from the image. If a
# host-side version skew is ever observed, the fix is a `make doctor` assertion
# naming the tool, not a new line in this file.
